# Default tag vocabulary for `arv tag`.
#
# Copied to <home>/config/tags.rec on first use; edit that copy freely. Each tag's
# Description is what the embedding model compares folders against, so write
# it as the kinds of things such a folder contains. Several phrasings help.
# Describe content, not the medium: words like "photos" or "files" make every
# photo folder look alike.
#
# Optional fields:
#   Alias   other words for the same tag (repeatable); when you type one while
#           reviewing it is replaced by the Name, so tags don't drift.
#   Match   file or folder name glob (repeatable): folders with such files get
#           the tag without any model (`arv tag --rules-only`).
#
# Tags may be namespaced as namespace:value, e.g. person:alice, place:kyoto,
# event:wedding-2019, source:pixel-7, project:weather-station. Namespaces keep
# facets apart (who, where, which occasion, which device) and export as
# hierarchical keywords (place|kyoto) with `arv keywords`. The Namespace records
# at the end declare them: what each holds, and whether a file has one value
# (Values: one, which a disc's layout can make folders of) or many.
#
# Known names (authority control): a namespaced tag can be an entry of its own,
# so that once confirmed it is recognised again (arv describe --ask makes them;
# arv tags show|add|label|alias|merge|split|retire KEY changes them, each an event):
#   Label      the preferred form now ("Anne Smith"); the key (Name) stays as made
#   Alias      other forms it is found as (also a merged entry's key)
#   Qualifier  what tells two of one name apart: dates, a relation, a place
#   Related    another entry or tag it goes with (software:kicad, electronics)
#   Same       the same entity elsewhere: wikidata:Q..., viaf:..., isni:..., geonames:...
#   Basis      why the entry was made: by whom, where, when
#   Private    yes: stays home, never on a public disc (people and families by default)
#   Retired    why it is withdrawn (kept, no longer offered)

%rec: Tag
%key: Name
%mandatory: Name
%allowed: Name Description Alias Match Label Qualifier Related Same Basis Private Retired

Name: family
Description: family life: relatives, children, babies, parents, grandparents, family gatherings at home
Alias: relatives
Alias: kids

Name: travel
Description: travel and holidays: trips, sightseeing, landmarks, temples, beaches, mountains, foreign cities and countries
Alias: holiday
Alias: holidays
Alias: trip
Alias: trips
Alias: vacation

Name: celebration
Description: celebrations and events: christmas, birthdays, weddings, anniversaries, parties, graduations
Alias: party
Alias: birthday
Alias: wedding
Alias: christmas

Name: pets
Description: pets and animals: cats, dogs, puppies, kittens, birds, horses
Alias: pet
Alias: cat
Alias: dog

Name: nature
Description: nature and outdoors: landscapes, gardens, flowers, hiking, wildlife, sunsets

Name: food
Description: food, cooking, recipes, restaurants, meals, baking
Alias: recipes
Alias: cooking

Name: vehicles
Description: cars, motorbikes, bicycles, trains, planes and other vehicles

Name: home
Description: house and home: renovation, furniture, rooms, moving house, garden projects
Alias: house
Alias: renovation

Name: people
Description: friends and people: portraits, groups, gatherings, reunions
Alias: friends

Name: work
Description: work and career: jobs, office, meetings, presentations, business documents
Alias: job
Alias: career

Name: school
Description: school and study: university, courses, homework, lecture notes, theses
Alias: study
Alias: university
Alias: uni

Name: code
Description: software source code and programming projects, scripts, repositories
Alias: software
Alias: programming
Alias: source
Match: *.git
Match: *.py
Match: *.c
Match: *.h
Match: *.cpp
Match: *.rs
Match: *.go
Match: *.js
Match: *.ts
Match: *.java
Match: Makefile
Match: CMakeLists.txt

Name: electronics
Description: electronics and hardware projects: circuits, schematics, PCBs, firmware, microcontrollers
Alias: hardware
Alias: pcb
Alias: firmware
Match: *.kicad_pcb
Match: *.kicad_sch
Match: *.sch
Match: *.brd
Match: *.gbr
Match: *.ino

Name: design
Description: design and art files: drawings, CAD models, 3D printing, graphics, illustrations
Alias: cad
Alias: art
Alias: 3d printing
Match: *.stl
Match: *.step
Match: *.scad
Match: *.f3d
Match: *.blend
Match: *.psd
Match: *.xcf
Match: *.kra

Name: music
Description: music and audio: songs, recordings, albums, podcasts, sound files
Alias: audio
Alias: songs
Match: *.flac
Match: *.mp3

Name: video
Description: video recordings, films, movies, home movies
Alias: videos
Alias: movies
Alias: films

Name: documents
Description: scanned documents and paperwork: letters, forms, manuals, receipts
Alias: paperwork
Alias: docs
Alias: scans

Name: legal
Description: legal and identity documents: contracts, certificates, passports, wills, deeds

Name: finance
Description: money and finance: bank statements, taxes, invoices, insurance, payslips
Alias: tax
Alias: taxes
Alias: bank
Alias: receipts

Name: health
Description: health and medical records, prescriptions, test results
Alias: medical

Name: backup
Description: backups and exports: phone backups, email archives, account exports, ISO files, zip archives
Alias: backups
Alias: exports
Match: *.mbox
Match: *.pst
Match: *.vhd
Match: *.vmdk
Match: *.qcow2

Name: games
Description: games and gaming: save files, mods, screenshots, game projects
Alias: gaming
Alias: saves

# Namespaces. Values: one means a file has one value: its own replaces its
# folder's, and `arv tags` lists a path given two. Values: many means any number. From says where a value may be
# suggested from: file-date is the file's own date (EXIF, or its time), right
# for a camera's photo, wrong for a scan of an old print.
%rec: Namespace
%key: Name
%mandatory: Name Values
%allowed: Name Description Values From
%type: Values enum one many

Name: date
Description: when the content is from, as an EDTF date or range: 2019-07, 1995/2008, 197X, 1995~
Values: one
From: file-date

Name: event
Description: the occasion: a trip, a wedding, a move
Values: one

Name: place
Description: where it is from; places nest, so a photo may be both kyoto and fushimi-inari
Values: many

Name: project
Description: the piece of work it belongs to
Values: one

Name: person
Description: who is in it, or who made it
Values: many

Name: family
Description: a family as a whole: its papers, its house, its gatherings
Values: many

Name: organisation
Description: a company, school, club, authority or charity it is from or about
Values: many

Name: software
Description: a program it is made with or about: an editor, a CAD tool, a game
Values: many

Name: work
Description: anything else made by others that it is about: a book, a film, an album
Values: many

Name: source
Description: what made it: a camera, a phone, a scanner, an account
Values: many

Name: role
Description: which copy of a scan or recording it is: raw (as captured), master (the copy to keep), access (made from the master for reading; can be made again)
Values: one
